{"id":"u-251f8989-a551-4973-80c6-a2325c09fc9c","src":"community","title":"Acceleration  Phase 2","author":"Amadeo Z.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/hYlICm-acceleration-phase-2","desc":"This program is built as a 3-day full body split, where every session combines functional movement patterns (push, pull, squat, hinge, lunge, carry, core) with progressive resistance training. The goal of this phase is not just to lift heavier weights, but to improve movement quality, control, and strength expression under tempo.\n\nBy combining tempo prescriptions with controlled rep ranges, you’re training both muscular function (joint stability, mind-muscle connection, movement efficiency) and strength progression (mechanical tension, load increases).\n\t•\tFunction: Exercises like lunges, split squats, box step-ups, and rows emphasize joint stability, unilateral balance, and athletic transfer.\n\t•\tWeight: Compound lifts (squat, bench, hack squat, RDL, split squat) allow you to progressively overload through volume, rep ranges, and eventual weight increases.\n\t•\tTempo & Rep Progression: Instead of relying only on adding load, progress is built by slowing eccentrics, pausing in weak points, and extending time under tension. This ensures muscle growth, tendon adaptation, and better control through the full ROM.\n\t•\tFull Body 3x/Week: Each day blends upper + lower + core/arms so you’re reinforcing functional strength patterns with higher frequency, while still emphasizing a slightly different focus per session (posterior chain, push + quads, legs + arms).\n\nThis Acceleration Phase (Phase 2) pushes past the foundation you built in Phase 1:\n\t•\tFrom “learning patterns and tempo control” → to executing with load, intent, and progression.\n\t•\tFrom “basic stability” → to strength under control.\n\t•\tFrom “weight as the only metric” → to tempo, time under tension, reps, and load as progressive tools.\n\n👉 In short: The purpose is to functionally strengthen the body under load with tempo discipline, creating muscle growth, control, and transferable strength — while preparing you for the next phase where speed and power expression will become even more important.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-15T02:15:38.268Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Legday","Upper Body","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":6.5},{"r":6,"rpe":7},{"r":6,"rpe":7.5}],"note":"3-0-2-2"},{"n":"Stiff Leg Deadlift","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":6},{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}],"note":"4-2-1-0"},{"n":"Split Squat Front Foot Elevated (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Bulgarian Splitt Squats Front Foot Elevated + Heel Elevated on a 1.5kg Platte (quad!!)\n3-2-1-0"},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"4-1-1-0"},{"n":"Squat (Paused)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":6},{"r":12,"rpe":7},{"r":12,"rpe":7.5}],"note":"6-2-1-0"},{"n":"Step-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Glute Focussed with one hand holding the Station for Balance and the other hand a Weight!\n2-0-1-0"},{"n":"Bike Ergometer cardiovascular","sets":[{"sec":1200,"secHi":1200,"rpe":10},{"sec":1200,"secHi":1200,"rpe":6}],"note":"8x Sets of 20 sec max Speed and 20sec Cool down/ 2Rounds  / 2min Break between Rounds!"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":6.5},{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":2}],"note":"3-1-1-1"},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":6.5},{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":2}],"note":"3-1-1-1"},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Single Arm)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":6},{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}],"note":"2-1-1-1"},{"n":"Underhand Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":6},{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}],"note":"3-1-1-1"},{"n":"Decline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7},{"r":10,"rpe":7.5},{"r":10,"rpe":8}],"note":"4-1-1-0"},{"n":"Incline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":6.5},{"r":12,"rpe":7,"x":